or capacity for self-renewal, and are often more limited in both senses.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0011026 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432>)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0011026 \"progenitor cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011026 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011115 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000034)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0011026 obo:CL_0011115)\n# Class: obo:CL_4030006 (fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1186/1477-7827-7-129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8080933\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube that secretes mucus and oviduct-specific products in response to hormonal stimulation from estrogen and luteinizing hormone. This fallopian tube secretory cell is similar in height to the ciliated cell, but typically exhibits a more narrow, columnar shape. Its nucleus is ovoid and oriented perpendicular to the cell's long axis, with denser chromatin and a smaller nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4030006 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4030006 \"2022-03-03T10:39:31Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"oviduct secretory epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"uterine tube secretory epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2013.10.013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030006 \"The other cell types of the fallopian tube epithelium include the ciliated cell and the intercalary cell, or peg cell. The fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell type has been implicated as a source of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030006 \"fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 obo:CL_1001591)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 obo:CL_4052019)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\n# Class: obo:CL_4030007 (fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4030007 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4030007 \"2022-03-08T12:40:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"oviduct ciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube ciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"uterine tube ciliated epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 obo:CL_0005012)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0007589))\n# Class: obo:CL_4033014 (peg cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2210508\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30023181\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033014 \"A small, narrow, peg-shaped epithelial cell with little cytoplasm that is part of oviduct epithelium. This cell is rarer than the ciliated and secretory epithelial cells of the fallopian tube epithelium and is often found intercalated between them. Peg cells are generally distributed basally along the epithelium and have been found in high concentrations at the fimbriated, distal end of the fallopian tube in humans. It may have a regenerative/stem-cell function. In humans, markers include EPCAM, CD44, and ITGA6.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033014 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033014 \"2023-02-02T15:07:12Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033014 \"FTE stem-like cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033014 \"FTESC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033014 \"fallopian tube epithelial stem-like cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033014 \"intercalary cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033014 \"In vitro evidence supports a stem-cell/regenerative function for these cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033014 \"peg cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4033014 obo:CL_4052019)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4033014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004804))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4033048 obo:CL_0011026)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4042021 obo:CL_0011026)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4042022 obo:CL_0011026)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4052006 obo:CL_0011026)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
