{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' ISSUE_COMMENTS.md && sed -n '1,240p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"Added the reviewed NTR as `CL:9900001` with label \"dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell\"; changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n## Summary\n\nAdded a new CL term for issue #3196:\n\n- `CL:9900001` dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe issue thread settled on \"dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell\" as the primary label, with UCFP/unclassified names retained as synonyms. I added the reviewed human fallopian tube progenitor concept as a new `CL_99xxxxx` term because no matching label or synonym was present in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n\nThe term is defined as a human fallopian tube epithelium progenitor with epithelial and endothelial marker features and potential to differentiate into fallopian tube ciliated and secretory epithelial cells. The logical definition uses:\n\n- `progenitor cell` (`CL:0011026`)\n- `part of` some `fallopian tube epithelium` (`UBERON:0003889`)\n- `in taxon` some `Homo sapiens` (`NCBITaxon:9606`)\n- `develops into` some `fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell` (`CL:4030006`)\n- `develops into` some `fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell` (`CL:4030007`)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- Checked `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` for existing matching terms and synonyms.\n- Checked the proposed parent/context terms already present in CL.\n- Checked DOSDP patterns for relevant compositional/taxon patterns.\n- Tried `aurelian fulltext PMID:40475517`, but `aurelian` is not installed in this environment.\n- Checked publication metadata using NCBI E-utilities for PMID:40475517 and Europe PMC/NCBI metadata for PMID:35320732.\n- Added contributor ORCID `0000-0002-1482-1032`, creator `GitHub Copilot`, date metadata, and the issue tracker annotation.\n- Ran `git diff --check`.\n\n## Validation\n\n`git diff --check` passed. Full ROBOT/OWL validation was not run because neither `robot` nor `owltools` is installed in this environment.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
